# Knowledge-base corpus for library search. Written for this repository.
{"id": "kb/maintenance-window", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "The maintenance window runs from 02:00 to 04:00 UTC every second Sunday. During the window the write API returns 503 and reads are served from a replica. Scheduled jobs are paused and resume automatically afterwards. Customers on the enterprise plan can request an alternative window with two weeks notice.", "title": "Maintenance window"}
{"id": "kb/refund-policy", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Refunds are issued to the original payment method within five working days. A refund cannot be issued against an authorisation that has not been captured. Partial refunds are tracked against a remaining balance held by the payment provider. Currency conversion is applied at the rate on the day of the refund, not the day of purchase.", "title": "Refund policy"}
{"id": "kb/token-lifetimes", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Access tokens expire after one hour and refresh tokens after thirty days. A refresh token is single use: exchanging it returns a new pair and invalidates the old one. Tokens are bound to the client that requested them. Revoking a client invalidates every token it issued.", "title": "Token lifetimes"}
{"id": "kb/rate-limits", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Rate limits apply per API key rather than per account. The default allowance is six hundred requests a minute, burstable to a thousand for ten seconds. Exceeding the limit returns 429 with a Retry-After header. Limits can be raised on request for enterprise plans.", "title": "Rate limits"}
{"id": "kb/data-retention", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Event logs are retained for thirty days and then archived to cold storage for a further year. Deleted records are purged from backups within thirty-five days. Audit records are kept for seven years to meet reporting obligations.", "title": "Data retention"}
{"id": "kb/webhook-delivery", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Webhooks are delivered at least once, so receivers must tolerate duplicates. Delivery is retried with exponential backoff for up to twenty-four hours. Each payload is signed, and the signature must be verified against the raw bytes.", "title": "Webhook delivery"}
{"id": "kb/sso-setup", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Single sign-on supports SAML 2.0 and OpenID Connect. Group membership can be mapped to roles during provisioning. Just-in-time provisioning creates an account on first successful sign-in. Disabling SSO leaves existing accounts intact.", "title": "SSO setup"}
{"id": "kb/export-formats", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Exports are available as CSV, JSON Lines and Parquet. Large exports are delivered as a signed download link valid for one hour. Column order is stable across versions so downstream parsers do not break.", "title": "Export formats"}
{"id": "kb/incident-severity", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "Severity one means a core flow is unavailable for many customers. Severity two covers degraded service or a broken secondary flow. Severity three is internal or cosmetic with a workaround. Anyone may raise severity; lowering it requires review.", "title": "Incident severity"}
{"id": "kb/sandbox-environment", "metadata": {"source": "kb"}, "text": "The sandbox mirrors production behaviour with synthetic data. Test card numbers always succeed or fail deterministically. Sandbox data is reset every Sunday, and sandbox keys cannot be used against production endpoints.", "title": "Sandbox environment"}
